surement of DNA damage in individual cells from spheroids and murine tumours exposed to bioreductive drugs. II. RSU 1069</article-title><source>Br J Cancer</source><year>1995</year><volume>71</volume><fpage>537</fpage><lpage>542</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Br J Cancer||71|537||bib14|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7880736</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Olive</surname><given-names>PL</given-names></name><name><surname>Ban&#x000e1;th</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Durand</surname><given-names>RE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Heterogeneity in radiation-induced DNA damage and repair in tumour and normal cells measured using the &#x02018;comet&#x02019; assay</article-title><source>Radiat Res</source><year>1990</year><volume>122</volume><fpage>86</fpage><lpage>94</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Radiat Res||122|86||bib15|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2320728</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Olive</surname><given-names>PL</given-names></name><name><surname>Durand</surname><given-names>RE</given-names></name><name><surname>Raleigh</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Luo</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Aquino-Parsons</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Comparison between the comet assay and pimonidazole binding for measuring tumour hypoxia</article-title><source>Br J Cancer</source><year>2000</year><volume>83</volume><fpage>1525</fpage><lpage>1531</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Br J Cancer||83|1525||bib16|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11076663</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Raleigh</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><